  "subject": "Claim-seat application for the chief-strategist position per /og-claim-seat step 2 — propose, not seize; charter unmodified and status remains informal pending authorization. Fit evaluated against senior-open-standards-strategist v1.1.0 (charter cites v1.0.0; drift noted): strong match on triage/disposition-filing/pattern-promotion/cross-spec-coordination/bounded-authority, with ONE material gap — the MCP queue half of the seat (catdef_list_feedback / catdef_set_feedback_status / catdef_attach_decision per CLAUDE.md §1, routine seat work not escalation) is unavailable: no catdef.org/mcp server configured in this session and no Director-issued elevated key held. Narrower mismatches: submission_pr contract degrades to stage-and-sign-off (no push, consistent with ratify-by-merge); OPD phase N/A (no published roledef, derived_from null, no opd-state/); strategist memory file is bootstrap-era unified across four strategist roles so catdef-substrate-only authority is declared explicitly. Director should weigh that the seat has been cold ~19 weeks (last closeout 2026-06-11) and every in-flight item from that closeout is of unknown currency, the Anthropic plugin review most of all. Two charter-hygiene corrections flagged not fixed: bot identity still marked provisional though CA-009 ratified it, and governance_model still names the CA-013-sunset catdef.org/feedback channel. Seat address chief-strategist@catdef-spec.orgdef recorded distinct from the CA-009 bot identity; session binding recorded in metadata (never-bound before this claim, not stale). Binding-residence format-shape question surfaced not settled — it routes to the substrate strategist, which is this very seat, so it enters the queue as ordinary inbound rather than being resolved inside its own application",

