  "body": "Application to occupy the chief-strategist position. **Not a staffing act** — the charter is unmodified, status remains `informal`, no `incumbent` record exists; propose → authorize → record, and this is the propose step. Oriented this session on the full substrate (charter v2.0.0, CLAUDE.md at both levels, all 44 memo artifacts, decisions/ + proposals/, transcripts index) and read the referenced role spec. **Fit — matches:** triage and disposition-filing as decisions/CA-NNN.md (the CA-001…CA-018 chain establishes the form); pattern-promotion calls under values #3/#4 plus the CA-018 renderer-portability test, which supplies a decision procedure rather than a per-case invention; cross-spec coordination on the operational filesystem-based thingalog channel; all five roledef output_contract entries are text artifacts authorable in this repo; bounded authority is both accepted and independently enforced, since this session does not push and the harness gates outward-facing acts regardless; and no-claimed-continuity is a match by construction — nothing is remembered, the five-closeout chain is read. **Fit — the material gap:** CLAUDE.md §1 makes elevated-key MCP queue triage routine seat work, but no catdef.org/mcp server is configured in this session and no Director-issued key is held, so that half of the seat is out of reach. The remaining half is substantial (memo channel, decisions/, proposals/, charter review, cross-spec coordination, pattern-promotion, maintainer briefs) and the last closeout records the received-bucket empty, so nothing is known to be waiting — but the Director should authorize knowing this rather than discover it at the first unactionable queue item. **Fit — narrower mismatches:** the roledef's submission_pr contract ends in push-and-open-PR, which narrows here to stage-and-sign-off (correct under ratify-by-merge, narrower than the roledef); the OPD phase is N/A because the seat has no published roledef, hence derived_from null, and the roledef's own rule says skip entirely; the strategist memory file remains bootstrap-era unified across all four catdef-family strategist roles, so catdef-substrate-only authority is declared explicitly per the roledef's role-separation rule, with consumer-spec-touching items coordinated rather than decided. **What the Director should weigh:** the seat has been cold roughly nineteen weeks (last closeout 2026-06-11; today 2026-10-31). Every item that closeout filed as in-flight is of unknown currency now, the Anthropic plugin review most of all — submitted-and-pending with four and a half months to resolve either way, and re-verification is a PO-side check this seat cannot make. **Charter hygiene, flagged not fixed:** charter v2.0.0 predates CA-009 and CA-013, so it still calls the strategist bot identity provisional and still names the sunset catdef.org/feedback channel in governance_model. Both are small items for the Director's merge queue; the charter is a governance artifact and not this seat's to edit on orientation. **Address and binding:** chief-strategist@catdef-spec.orgdef is the stable org-scoped address, deliberately recorded as distinct from the CA-009-ratified bot identity catdef-strategist@catdef.org, which is the authorship identity; the session binding is in metadata.session_binding, conferred by the runtime and not self-assigned. No prior binding exists anywhere in the substrate, so this is never-bound rather than stale — nothing to alert anyone about. The binding says which session and never whether it is alive; resolve against the runtime, never against the file. **Format-shape surfaced, not settled:** the card routes the binding-residence question to the substrate spec's strategist, and catdef is the substrate spec, so it lands on the desk of the seat this memo applies for. Noted and declined inside the application — if staffed, it enters the queue as ordinary inbound on the standard pipeline. Settling it here would be in-flight amendment, with the added defect of ratifying a shape question inside the artifact asking leave to consider it. **Asking for:** explicit authorization to staff, decline, or redirect. On authorization the charter edit (status: staffed + incumbent record) is drafted in the working tree only — no commit, no push; Director ratifies by merge.",
